# Development Rule

## Phase 0 — Branch Creation (MANDATORY BEFORE ANY FILE CHANGES)

**This is the first action. No file may be created or modified until the branch exists.**

```bash
# For features:
git checkout -b feat/[TICKET-ID]-[short-description]

# For bug fixes:
git checkout -b fix/[TICKET-ID]-[short-description]

# For chores/deps/docs:
git checkout -b chore/[TICKET-ID]-[short-description]
```

Gate checks before creating the branch:
- [ ] `docs/designs/[TICKET-ID]-requirements.md` exists
- [ ] `docs/designs/[TICKET-ID]-design.md` exists (or user has explicitly approved inline design)

If either doc is missing: **STOP. Run the requirements or design phase first.**

If a branch for this ticket already exists, check it out instead of creating a new one:
```bash
git branch | grep [TICKET-ID]   # check if it exists
git checkout feat/[TICKET-ID]-... # check it out
```

**Never do ticket work on the default branch (main, master, develop, or any integration branch).** If you realise you are on the wrong branch after making changes, use `git stash`, switch to the feature branch, and `git stash pop` before creating any commits.

